  "title": "OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al. 2019)",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted derivative dataset of steady-state visually evoked potential (SSVEP) EEG recordings from 54 subjects across 2 sessions. This dataset contains 21,600 trials of 4-second EEG recordings sampled at 1000 Hz from 62 channels, designed for brain-computer interface benchmarking using SSVEP stimulation paradigms. The data has been standardized and organized using the Mother of All BCI Benchmarks (MOABB) framework to facilitate reproducible analysis and cross-study comparison.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were recorded from 54 subjects performing SSVEP-based tasks across 2 sessions. Each trial consisted of 4-second recordings at 1000 Hz sampling frequency from 62 EEG channels. The paradigm included 4 classes of SSVEP stimulation.",
